  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a given circuit diagram, a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> zener diode along with a series resistance is connected across a&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;power supply. The minimum value of the resistance required, if the maximum zener current is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math> will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#937;.</mtext></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0120_fac97a4e01d7.png\" style=\"width: 433px; height: 192px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "500",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0120_fac97a4e01d7.png\" style=\"width: 433px; height: 192px;\" /></p><p>Voltage across,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">L</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Also, voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></math> volt</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mrow><mn>90</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Current in zener diode is maximum when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"\"><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p>"
  }
}